  "learningBlocks": [
    {
      "id": "l24-b1",
      "type": "concept",
      "title": "ut does not mean 'purpose' by itself",
      "learnerCopy": {
        "en": "An ut-clause can express purpose, result, desired outcome or other subordinate relationships. Lesson 24 asks what the main clause makes the ut-clause mean.",
        "fr": "Une proposition en ut peut exprimer le but, le résultat, un résultat désiré ou d'autres relations. La leçon 24 demande ce que la principale fait signifier à la subordonnée en ut."
      },
      "referenceIds": [
        "grammar-nunn-1922",
        "grammar-scanlon-1944",
        "grammar-petitmangin-1930",
        "curriculum-latin-course-40-v1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "l24-b2",
      "type": "authentic-example",
      "title": "Ut digni efficiamur",
      "sourceId": "marian-versicle-digni-l24",
      "learnerCopy": {
        "en": "Ora pro nobis ... ut digni efficiamur gives the desired outcome of the prayer: pray for us so that we may be made worthy. digni agrees with the understood 'we'; efficiamur is subjunctive of efficio.",
        "fr": "Ora pro nobis ... ut digni efficiamur exprime le résultat désiré de la prière : priez pour nous afin que nous soyons rendus dignes. digni s'accorde avec le « nous » sous-entendu ; efficiamur est le subjonctif de efficio."
      },
      "referenceIds": [
        "marian-versicle-digni-l24",
        "grammar-nunn-1922",
        "grammar-scanlon-1944",
        "grammar-petitmangin-1930",
        "curriculum-latin-course-40-v1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "l24-b3",
      "type": "result",
      "title": "Sic ... ut marks consequence",
      "sourceId": "vulg-jn3-16-l24",
      "learnerCopy": {
        "en": "Sic enim Deus dilexit mundum, ut Filium... daret links degree/manner in the main clause to its consequence: God so loved the world that He gave His Son. This is not the same relation as a simple command done for a purpose.",
        "fr": "Sic enim Deus dilexit mundum, ut Filium... daret relie le degré de la principale à sa conséquence : Dieu a tant aimé le monde qu'il a donné son Fils. Ce rapport n'est pas celui d'un simple acte accompli dans un but."
      },
      "referenceIds": [
        "vulg-jn3-16-l24",
        "grammar-nunn-1922",
        "grammar-scanlon-1944",
        "grammar-petitmangin-1930",
        "curriculum-latin-course-40-v1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "l24-b4",
      "type": "comparison",
      "title": "magis and plus compare",
      "learnerCopy": {
        "en": "magis and plus both express 'more', but they appear in different constructions. Beatius est magis dare... compares actions; diligis me plus his? expresses degree/comparison.",
        "fr": "magis et plus expriment tous deux « davantage », mais dans des constructions différentes. Beatius est magis dare... compare des actions ; diligis me plus his? exprime un degré ou une comparaison."
      },
      "referenceIds": [
        "grammar-nunn-1922",
        "grammar-scanlon-1944",
        "grammar-petitmangin-1930",
        "curriculum-latin-course-40-v1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "l24-b5",
      "type": "degree",
      "title": "tantum and nimis express degree",
      "learnerCopy": {
        "en": "tantum can mean so much/so great or only depending on context; nimis intensifies strongly. These degree words are useful because result clauses often depend on an expressed degree.",
        "fr": "tantum peut signifier « tant / si grand » ou « seulement » selon le contexte ; nimis intensifie fortement. Ces mots de degré sont utiles car les propositions de résultat dépendent souvent d'un degré exprimé."
      },
      "referenceIds": [
        "grammar-nunn-1922",
        "grammar-scanlon-1944",
        "grammar-petitmangin-1930",
        "curriculum-latin-course-40-v1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "l24-b6",
      "type": "retrieval",
      "title": "Ask a semantic question",
      "learnerCopy": {
        "en": "For each ut-clause ask: intended goal, actual/logical result, or desired prayer outcome? Then verify subjunctive morphology and any degree-correlative words.",
        "fr": "Pour chaque proposition en ut, demandez : but voulu, résultat logique/réel ou résultat désiré de la prière ? Vérifiez ensuite le subjonctif et les mots corrélatifs de degré."
      },
      "referenceIds": [
        "grammar-nunn-1922",
        "grammar-scanlon-1944",
        "grammar-petitmangin-1930",
        "curriculum-latin-course-40-v1"
      ]
    }
  ],
